extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 129-131 (cache p129-p131, page_offset 0); the lore opens at the foot of 129, the abilities and first O.C.C. Skills are on 130, the rest of the block on 131. Printed 130 checked against a 110 dpi render; the OCR agreed on every number. No plains-borg class was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the ladder on printed 192 for this O.C.C., read off a render, as briefed. || GROUP: filed under the Silver River Republics'' O.C.C.s with no group heading; stored as men-of-arms (a combat cyborg). mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || BODY AND ATTRIBUTES: 280 M.D.C. as mdc_base; P.S. 26, P.P. 22 and Spd 176 as fixed attribute_dice, the Destroyer ''Borg precedent from this book. The book prints no M.D.C. by location. Mental attributes and P.B. are the character''s own. Not supersedes_race: the book converts gauchos, the brain is the character''s own, and a humanoid race''s pools and dice win a pairing as for every other cyborg O.C.C.; played as a human (no R.C.C.), everything applies as printed. This is the class-check warning about attribute_dice, mdc_base and starting_money, and it is accepted as correct. || BONUSES: +2 parry, dodge and roll with punch/impact, +1 pull punch, +4 save vs horror factor stored unconditionally; the book does not call them totals, so the P.P. 22 attribute bonus is added on top by the sheet. The +1 strike with a long-range weapon is conditional and is an ability. || SKILLS: identical to the Gaucho''s list except Horsemanship +15 (General 40+15), Tracking +10 (Tracking (people) 25+10) and Wilderness Survival +10 (30+10). Spanish 98 as Language: Spanish; Literacy: Spanish (+15%) as Literacy: Native Language 40+15; Basic Math 45+10; Detect Ambush 30+10; one Pilot +10; W.P. Knife, W.P. Bola (treat as Archery & Targeting, in its note), two W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert converts to Martial Arts or Assassin (if evil) for one other skill. || RELATED: six, plus one W.P. and one skill at level 3, two at 6, one at 9 and 12 (2/2/1/1; the W.P. half is the note). Bonuses as printed: Communications +10, Domestic +10, Pilot +10, Pilot Related +10, Rogue +2, Technical +5, Wilderness +10; Science and W.P. any; the Electrical, Espionage, Mechanical, Medical and Physical limits as the Gaucho''s; Military none. No Horsemanship or Cowboy line, so neither category is granted. || SECONDARY: five, limited as the related list, no bonuses, no schedule. || EQUIPMENT: an energy rifle of choice and one more energy weapon of choice from catalog sets led by this book''s Silver River weapons; eight E-clips (four per weapon); vibro-knife; one non-energy weapon of choice from a catalog set; survival knife; camp equipment as tent and sleeping bag; poncho or cloak as a choice. Not stored, no catalog row and not stubbed: the light cyborg infantry armor (270 M.D.C., in an ability), the two energy bolas (no stats printed here; the plain Bola row is not a substitute) and the wide-brimmed hat (the catalog''s large-brim hats are Palladium Fantasy, Heroes Unlimited and Nightbane rows). || MONEY: 1D6x1000 credits. || CYBERNETICS: the book says ''see above''; the built-in systems and the three-plus-three picks are abilities, the app having no implant pick."
