## Lore

Cordoba and Santiago have the technology to make full bionic conversion
common, and a number of gauchos have given up their humanity for it. Some were
crippled in battle or by accident and rebuilt, some volunteered to become
defenders of the land, and a few are survivors of Larhold raids who want
revenge. Built to ride the range on robot horses, cyber-horses or hover cycles,
these ''cyber-gauchos'' are lightly armored compared to Coalition cyborgs but
fast, well coordinated and full of concealed weapons, and they often hide their
metal bodies under ponchos, capes and hats.

They are the terror of the Larhold barbarians, hunting the raiders without
mercy, and the Larhold return the favour: a captured ''borg is stripped of its
bionics piece by piece, so most fight to the death rather than be taken. On the
plains they favour long, heavy energy weapons, luring pursuers into a chase and
shooting them from beyond the range of Larhold bows.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'plains-borg');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
